# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:05:42+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 229  Severity: high
# Type: xss

## Root Cause
User-provided data is being rendered directly without escaping, allowing potential XSS attacks.

## Explanation
The patch uses a secure method to escape the `danger` message before rendering it. This prevents any malicious scripts from being executed in the user's browser, thereby securing the application against XSS vulnerabilities.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
         res.render('app/bulkproducts',{messages:{danger:'Invalid file'},legacy:true})
     }else{
-        res.render('app/bulkproducts',{messages:{danger:'Invalid file'},legacy:true})
+        res.render('app/bulkproducts',{messages:{danger: escapeHtml('Invalid file')},legacy:true})
     }

